// ── Replicable key: ONE rule and ONE wording for every form that mints a token key ──
// CA create, CA CSR, the rekey section and the Inventory HSM request all mint a key, and
// whether that key may ever leave this token is decided at that moment and never again
// (CKA_EXTRACTABLE is fixed at generation). Four forms saying that four ways, or enabling
// the box under four different rules, is the drift this console keeps being reported for,
// so the words, the rule and the value all come from here. Every algorithm these forms offer
// can be minted replicable; the server (pkcs11_replicable_refusal) refuses anything else.
// ── Profile picker: the key-in-browser and CSR forms name a profile the same way ──
// The first option names none, and the server then resolves it as for any protocol: the
// profile you hold, or all of yours combined. The key-in-HSM form deliberately has no picker
